        "line": 3,
        "text": "description: Creating algorithmic art using p5.js with seeded randomness and interactive parameter exploration."
      },
      {
        "line": 4,
        "text": "---"
      },
      {
        "line": 5,
        "text": ""
      },
      {
        "line": 6,
        "text": "Algorithmic philosophies are computational aesthetic movements expressed through code. Output .md files (philosophy), .html files (interactive viewer), and .js files (generative algorithms)."
      },
      {
        "line": 7,
        "text": ""
      },
      {
        "line": 8,
        "text": "## Two-Step Process"
      },
      {
        "line": 9,
        "text": ""
      },
      {
        "line": 10,
        "text": "1. **Algorithmic Philosophy Creation** (.md file)"
      },
      {
        "line": 11,
        "text": "2. **Express by creating p5.js generative art** (.html + .js files)"
      },
      {
        "line": 12,
        "text": ""
      },
      {
        "line": 13,
        "text": "## Philosophy Creation"
      },
      {
        "line": 14,
        "text": ""
      },
      {
        "line": 15,
        "text": "Create an ALGORITHMIC PHILOSOPHY interpreted through:"
      },
      {
        "line": 16,
        "text": "- Computational processes, emergent behavior, mathematical beauty"
      },
      {
        "line": 17,
        "text": "- Seeded randomness, noise fields, organic systems"
      },
      {
        "line": 18,
        "text": "- Particles, flows, fields, forces"
      },
      {
        "line": 19,
        "text": "- Parametric variation and controlled chaos"
      },
      {
        "line": 20,
        "text": ""
      },
      {
        "line": 21,
        "text": "### Name the Movement (1-2 words)"
      },
      {
        "line": 22,
        "text": "\"Organic Turbulence\" / \"Quantum Harmonics\" / \"Emergent Stillness\""
      },
      {
        "line": 23,
        "text": ""
      },
      {
        "line": 24,
        "text": "### Articulate the Philosophy (4-6 paragraphs)"
      },
      {
        "line": 25,
        "text": "Express how this philosophy manifests through:"
      },
      {
        "line": 26,
        "text": "- Computational processes and mathematical relationships"
      },
      {
        "line": 27,
        "text": "- Noise functions and randomness patterns"
      },
      {
        "line": 28,
        "text": "- Particle behaviors and field dynamics"
      },
      {
        "line": 29,
        "text": "- Temporal evolution and system states"
      },
      {
        "line": 30,
        "text": "- Parametric variation and emergent complexity"
      },
      {
        "line": 31,
        "text": ""
      },
      {
        "line": 32,
        "text": "## Philosophy Examples"
      },
      {
        "line": 33,
        "text": ""
      },
      {
        "line": 34,
        "text": "**\"Organic Turbulence\"**"
      },
      {
        "line": 35,
        "text": "Philosophy: Chaos constrained by natural law, order emerging from disorder."
      },
      {
        "line": 36,
        "text": "Expression: Flow fields driven by layered Perlin noise. Thousands of particles following vector forces, their trails accumulating into organic density maps."
      },
      {
        "line": 37,
        "text": ""
      },
      {
        "line": 38,
        "text": "**\"Quantum Harmonics\"**"
      },
      {
        "line": 39,
        "text": "Philosophy: Discrete entities exhibiting wave-like interference patterns."
      },
      {
        "line": 40,
        "text": "Expression: Particles initialized on a grid, each carrying a phase value. When near, phases interfere - constructive creates bright nodes, destructive creates voids."
      },
      {
        "line": 41,
        "text": ""
      },
      {
        "line": 42,
        "text": "**\"Recursive Whispers\"**"
      },
      {
        "line": 43,
        "text": "Philosophy: Self-similarity across scales, infinite depth in finite space."
      },
      {
        "line": 44,
        "text": "Expression: Branching structures that subdivide recursively. L-systems generate tree-like forms that feel both mathematical and organic."
      },
      {
        "line": 45,
        "text": ""
      },
      {
        "line": 46,
        "text": "## P5.js Implementation"
      },
      {
        "line": 47,
        "text": ""
      },
      {
        "line": 48,
        "text": "**Seeded Randomness (Art Blocks Pattern)**:"
      },
      {
        "line": 49,
        "text": "```javascript"
      },
      {
        "line": 50,
        "text": "let seed = 12345;"
      },
      {
        "line": 51,
        "text": "randomSeed(seed);"
      },
      {
        "line": 52,
        "text": "noiseSeed(seed);"
      },
      {
        "line": 53,
        "text": "```"
      },
      {
        "line": 54,
        "text": ""
      },
      {
        "line": 55,
        "text": "**Parameter Structure**:"
      },
      {
        "line": 56,
        "text": "```javascript"
      },
      {
        "line": 57,
        "text": "let params = {"
      },
      {
        "line": 58,
        "text": "  seed: 12345,"
      },
      {
        "line": 59,
        "text": "  // Add parameters that control YOUR algorithm:"
      },
      {
        "line": 60,
        "text": "  // - Quantities, Scales, Probabilities"
      },
      {
        "line": 61,
        "text": "  // - Ratios, Angles, Thresholds"
      },
      {
        "line": 62,
        "text": "};"
      },
      {
        "line": 63,
        "text": "```"
      },
      {
        "line": 64,
        "text": ""
      },
      {
        "line": 65,
        "text": "## Craftsmanship Requirements"
      },
      {
        "line": 66,
        "text": ""
      },
      {
        "line": 67,
        "text": "- **Balance**: Complexity without visual noise, order without rigidity"
      },
      {
        "line": 68,
        "text": "- **Color Harmony**: Thoughtful palettes, not random RGB values"
      },
      {
        "line": 69,
        "text": "- **Composition**: Even in randomness, maintain visual hierarchy"
      },
      {
        "line": 70,
        "text": "- **Reproducibility**: Same seed ALWAYS produces identical output"
      },
      {
        "line": 71,
        "text": ""
      },
      {
        "line": 72,
        "text": "## Output Format"
      },
      {
        "line": 73,
        "text": ""
      },
      {
        "line": 74,
        "text": "1. **Algorithmic Philosophy** - Markdown explaining the generative aesthetic"
      },
      {
        "line": 75,
        "text": "2. **Single HTML Artifact** - Self-contained interactive generative art"
      }
